# Purser UI — BUILD-TIME configuration (Vite env vars, baked into the bundle).
# Copy to `.env.local` to override for local `npm run dev` / `npm run build`.
# All are OPTIONAL. With none set the UI talks to the REAL control-plane REST API
# on the same origin (production-safe default).
#
# NOTE: these are baked at build time. To configure a BUILT container without
# rebuilding, use the runtime env vars instead (PURSER_API_BASE_URL,
# PURSER_GATEWAY_BASE_URL, PURSER_UI_MOCK) — the entrypoint writes them into
# env.js at container start. See ui/README.md.

# Backend mode. Unset => REAL HTTP client (default).
# Set to 1/true/on/yes to OPT IN to the in-memory mock (offline dev/demo only —
# it serves fabricated data, so never enable it in production).
# VITE_PURSER_MOCK=1

# Control-plane management API base (same origin by default).
# VITE_PURSER_API_BASE=/api/v1

# OpenAI-compatible Gateway base for the Playground. May live on another
# host/port than the control plane that serves this UI.
# VITE_PURSER_GATEWAY_BASE=/v1
# VITE_PURSER_GATEWAY_BASE=https://gateway.internal:8443/v1
